studio: fm, the thing at its cursor in ed, and a shell
  Lines stack down, the lines under one go across, and the lines under
  those down again. Each line is a slot, and a share such as 70% is its
  part of its parent; the rest of the line is what runs in it, and a
  slot that names nothing keeps a shell. ed -f edits whatever fm's cursor
  is on; a slot that runs studio show adds the lenses, diff, figure and
  run. A slot's name is how a program reaches it: studio send shell make
  types make into the shell, and studio read shell reads it.
top     70%
  fm    40%  fm
  ed         ed -f
shell
